syncthing source for Keel Linux
================================

Layout
------

This repository carries the full upstream source of Syncthing, the
continuous file synchronization program, with the debian/ packaging of
Keel Linux on top. The master branch holds both, as two commits per
release: the import of the upstream release source and the packaging.

Upstream source
---------------

The upstream source is the release tarball
syncthing-source-<version>.tar.gz of
https://github.com/syncthing/syncthing/releases, verified against the
sha256 digest the release publishes. The tarball carries the Go
modules under vendor/, so the build never touches the network.

Build
-----

The build needs Go 1.26.2, a pinned tool on the build host at
/usr/local/go1.26 (docs/build.md of this repository). Debian trixie
ships golang 1.24, which is too old for go.mod. With that on PATH:

    debuild -us -uc

Build-Depends has no golang entry on purpose: the toolchain is the
pinned tool of the build host, not an apt package. debian/rules puts
/usr/local/go1.26/bin at the front of PATH.

Tests
-----

tests/run.sh checks the packaging (no network-fetched build
dependencies, the vendor build flag) and, after a build, the .deb:
its fields, its contents and the binary itself, including a short run
that listens on a test port. See tests/run.sh.

The upstream test suite is not run at package build time: it is long
and parts of it need the network or a browser. The binary the package
ships is what tests/run.sh exercises.

What the package ships
----------------------

Only /usr/bin/syncthing and the documentation (README.md, LICENSE and
this notice). The systemd service, the system user and the
configuration are shipped by the keel-overlay-syncthing overlay, not
by this package (handbook decision 0050).
